1db5|n|The act of obeying, or the state of being obedient; compliance with that which is required by authority; subjection to rightful restraint or control. ; Words or actions denoting submission to authority; dutifulness. ; A following; a body of adherents; as, the Roman Catholic obedience, or the whole body of persons who submit to the authority of the pope. ; A cell (or offshoot of a larger monastery) governed by a prior. ; One of the three monastic vows. ; The written precept of a superior in a religious order or congregation to a subject.	a:85h,103,3~85h,103,3
1dbt|n|To give ear to; to execute the commands of; to yield submission to; to comply with the orders of. ; To submit to the authority of; to be ruled by. ; To yield to the impulse, power, or operation of; as, a ship obeys her helm. ; To give obedience.	a:1431,9,1~1431,9,1
1dbt|v|To give ear to; to execute the commands of; to yield submission to; to comply with the orders of. ; To submit to the authority of; to be ruled by. ; To yield to the impulse, power, or operation of; as, a ship obeys her helm. ; To give obedience.	d:1431,19,2~1431,19,2
