1ddi|n|The act of obligating. ; That which obligates or constrains; the binding power of a promise, contract, oath, or vow, or of law; that which constitutes legal or moral duty. ; Any act by which a person becomes bound to do something to or for anouther, or to forbear something; external duties imposed by law, promise, or contract, by the relations of society, or by courtesy, kindness, etc. ; The state of being obligated or bound; the state of being indebted for an act of favor or kindness; as, to place others under obligations to one. ; A bond with a condition annexed, and a penalty for nonfulfillment. In a larger sense, it is an acknowledgment of a duty to pay a certain sum or do a certain things.	a:pk3,84,86;1av9,72,11;15ne,70,50;1sij,57,4;1vto,45,8;1wie,41,5;rsg,39,3;wz,30,4;1luk,29,4;sx8,24,2~pk3,84,86;15ne,70,50;1av9,72,11;1w1v,3,10;1vto,45,8;ei,17,7;1wie,41,5;wz,30,4;1sij,57,4;1luk,29,4	v:20za,21,4~20za,21,4	N:28i1,55,2~28i1,55,2
